  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#38684\", \"PowerToys#42103\", \"PowerToys#41852\"], \"answer\": \"Requests for a standalone Command Palette, installable without the rest of PowerToys, have been filed before. The main thread is PowerToys#38684, and #42103 was pointed to it as a duplicate. #41852 covers the same idea as a 'graduation to standalone app' proposal. A maintainer ([user]) said in #38684 that the team will probably do this at some point. Command Palette is already a separate MSIX package, and the plan is for the standalone and PowerToys-bundled versions to share the same identity, so settings and extensions carry over. The archive shows no ready-made official zip or portable build yet. Please add your use case (non-admin users) and a link to your zip as a comment on #38684 instead of opening a new request. Your zip is an unofficial workaround, so users should treat it with the usual caution. For now, install Command Palette through PowerToys, or watch #38684 for an official standalone release.\"}",
